<title>NETHERLANDS: IHC Caland wins Penta-Ocean order.</title>
<headline>IHC Caland wins Penta-Ocean order.</headline>
<dateline>SCHIEDAM, Netherlands 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipbuilding and engineering group IHC Caland NV said on Tuesday it had won an order to build a suction dredger for Japan's Penta-Ocean Construction Co Ltd for more than 200 million guilders.</p>
<p>The ship will be delivered in the spring of 1999, IHC Caland said in a statement.</p>
<p>On Monday, the Dutch group announced it had won two other contracts worth a total of about 175 million guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
